<title>USA: Sears, Orchard Supply deal clears hurdle.</title>
<headline>Sears, Orchard Supply deal clears hurdle.</headline>
<dateline>HOFFMAN ESTATES, Ill. 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sears, Roebuck and Co said Monday the Hart-Scott-Rodino antitrust waiting period had expired for its planned acquisition of Orchard Supply Hardware Stores Corp.  </p>
<p>About 1.1 million shares of common stock of Orchard were tendered as of September 6, 1996, pursuant.</p>
<p>In August, Sears offered $35 for each share of San Jose, California-based Orchard, which operates 61 medium-sized hardware stores.</p>
<p>--Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
